      "review.claude.faq1.answer": "Yes, Claude consistently outperforms ChatGPT on coding benchmarks like SWE-bench. Claude 3.5 Sonnet is particularly strong at understanding complex codebases, debugging, and writing production-quality code. The larger context window (200K vs 128K) also helps when working with large projects.",
      "review.claude.faq1.question": "Is Claude better than ChatGPT for coding?",
      "review.claude.faq2.answer": "No, Claude does not have built-in web browsing capabilities. Its knowledge comes from its training data with a cutoff date. For tasks requiring current information, you would need to provide that information directly or use ChatGPT/Gemini which have web access.",
      "review.claude.faq2.question": "Can Claude access the internet?",
      "review.claude.faq3.answer": "Claude has a 200,000 token context window - the largest among mainstream AI assistants. This means it can process roughly 150,000 words or 500+ pages of text in a single conversation, making it ideal for analyzing entire codebases, books, or long documents.",
      "review.claude.faq3.question": "What is Claude's context window?",
      "review.claude.faq4.answer": "No, Claude cannot generate images. Unlike ChatGPT (which has DALL-E) or Gemini (which has Imagen), Claude is purely a text-based AI. However, it can analyze and describe images you upload, and can create SVGs and code-based visualizations through Artifacts.",
      "review.claude.faq4.question": "Can Claude generate images?",
      "review.claude.faq5.answer": "Artifacts is Claude's feature for creating and previewing content in a dedicated panel alongside the chat. You can generate interactive React components, SVG graphics, HTML/CSS previews, documents, and more. It's particularly useful for developers who want to see code output immediately.",
